      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing engages your parasympathetic nervous system, often called the \"rest and digest\" system. This deliberate slowing of your breath signals to your body that you are safe, which counteracts the \"fight or flight\" response triggered by stress. Consequently, this can help downregulate the release of stress hormones like cortisol, leading to a calmer physiological state.",
      "source": "target",
